You are tasked with writing a Python command-line script from scratch.
Build a self-contained script for Termux (Android, Python 3) that translates
Farsi (Persian) text found in files to English, processing files in parallel.
Follow these specifications. **Purpose:** Walk a directory tree (or accept a
single file) and detect Farsi/Persian text in plain-text source and
documentation files.
Translate the Farsi content to English using a Google Translate wrapper, writing
results to new output files without modifying the originals. **Dependencies:**
`deep_translator` (GoogleTranslator), `loguru` for logging, `tqdm` for progress
bars.
Use only the standard library otherwise (`argparse`, `json`, `re`, `sys`,
`time`, `concurrent.futures.ProcessPoolExecutor`/`as_completed`,
`multiprocessing.Pool`, `pathlib`, `typing`).
Include a Termux-compatible shebang line
(`/data/data/com.termux/files/usr/bin/env python`) and `from __future__ import
annotations`. **Constants to define:** - A Farsi detection regex covering the
Arabic-script Unicode blocks U+0600–U+06FF, U+0750–U+077F, and U+08A0–U+08FF. -
A tuple of text "break markers" used to split long text into translatable
chunks, ordered from preferred to fallback: newline, CRLF, sentence endings
followed by double space, semicolon-space, comma-space, and single space. - A
regex matching runs of whitespace and sentence punctuation (for in-place line
handling). - Default file suffixes: `.txt`, `.md`, `.py`, `.json`, `.csv`. -
Default excluded directory/name patterns: `lazy`, `.git`, `__pycache__`,
`.mypy_cache`, `.ruff_cache`, `.pytest_cache`. **Helper functions:** 1.
`read_text_any_encoding(path)`: try reading with utf-8, then latin-1, cp1252,
iso-8859-1; skip on `OSError`/`UnicodeDecodeError`; if all fail, raise `OSError`
with a clear message. 2. `contains_farsi(text)`: return whether the Farsi regex
matches anywhere. 3. `derive_output_path(src, suffix)`: return a sibling path
named `<stem>_<suffix><original suffix>`. 4.
Chunking logic: split text into chunks under a maximum length (for
GoogleTranslator's limit) by repeatedly trying the break markers in priority
order, falling back to hard splits when no marker is found.
Preserve original separators so reassembly is faithful. 5.
Translation of a chunk via `GoogleTranslator(source="auto" or "fa",
target="en")`, with retry logic: on failure, retry a limited number of times
with a short sleep (`time.sleep`) between attempts, then log via loguru and fall
back to returning the original text for that chunk. 6.
File discovery: recursively walk a root directory, filter by suffix and skip any
path containing excluded names; accept a single file argument as well. **Main
behavior:** - Parse CLI arguments with `argparse`: a required path (file or
directory), options for output suffix (default something like `en`), allowed
suffixes, extra excludes, max chunk length, number of worker processes, retry
count/delay, a dry-run or list-only mode, and a verbosity/log-file option. - For
each candidate file, read it, check `contains_farsi`; skip files without Farsi.
For files with Farsi, translate line-by-line or chunk-by-chunk, preserving
non-Farsi content, indentation, and line structure.
Write the result to the derived output path (never overwrite the source).
Skip files whose output already exists unless a force flag is given. -
Parallelism: use `ProcessPoolExecutor` (or `multiprocessing.Pool`) to process
files concurrently across the configured worker count, collecting results with
`as_completed`.
Wrap the iteration in `tqdm` to show progress. - Logging: use `loguru` with
INFO-level summaries per file and DEBUG details; errors per file must not crash
the whole run—catch exceptions per file, log them, and continue. - Output a
final summary: counts of files scanned, translated, skipped (no Farsi / already
exists), and failed, plus elapsed time. - Exit codes: 0 on full success, nonzero
if any file failed; handle `KeyboardInterrupt` gracefully and exit with a clean
message. **Edge cases to handle:** files with mixed encodings or undecodable
bytes; empty files; very long single lines with no break markers (hard-split);
Farsi appearing only in code comments or string literals (translate the whole
text chunk anyway, but keep the file valid as text); network failures during
translation (retry, then fall back to original text); paths with spaces or
Unicode; symlinks (avoid infinite recursion); a root path that doesn't exist
(clear error and nonzero exit); and rate-limit/timeout errors from the
translation service. **Usage:** Run as `python script.py <path> [options]`, with
`--help` documenting every option.
Make the script executable with the Termux shebang and include a `if __name__ ==
"__main__":` entry point that calls a `main()` function returning an exit code,
passed to `sys.exit`. ---
